  "body": "## The rule decided\n\nOption 1, the lean rule the issue suggested, implemented at the salt: **a change of generator output that fixes a defect makes old caches stale.**\n\nA named constant `GENERATOR_OUTPUT_VERSION` (`crates/app/src/operation/stamp.rs`) is written into every operation stamp. The PR that changes what a generator emits - a moved start, dive, lead, level or entry, any emitted move - bumps the number in the same PR. Every cache a project saved under the old number reads Stale once and clears on regenerate. A refactor whose output is byte-identical does not bump it. No auto-detection: the manual bump is the rule.\n\nPR #3684 is exactly such a change, so a project saved before it now reads Stale instead of posting the old 18 mm plunge at the first tab window (#3453). The rule text sits in the stamp comment at the salt and in `docs/decisions/3704-generator-output-version.md`.\n\nDropped: option 2 (the wrong path would post silently, which the Prime Directive refuses); auto-detecting output changes (heavy, can miss); a per-kind version (every future fix would re-decide the scope; one number is the lean rule).\n\n## The one-time churn\n\nThe term moves every stamp once, the same churn the v3/v4 salt bumps produced. It moves more than the saved stamps: the refreshed caches also hold regenerated moves, regenerated parameters and the current project-file version. So the committed project goldens were refreshed, catalog cases with `cargo xtask catalog`, the guide examples with their suites' `WRITE_GOLDEN=1` runs. Every `.nc` golden is byte-identical: the generator output of the current tree does not change.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nEvery changed project under `examples/` (the 15 catalog cases plus the 3 guide examples). Each row: stamp + cache refresh by the version bump; `.nc` byte-identical in all rows.\n\n- `examples/catalog/2d/adaptive-pocket/adaptive-pocket.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh; pocket cached moves regenerated\n- `examples/catalog/2d/contour-tabs/contour-tabs.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh\n- `examples/catalog/2d/drill-overfeed/drill-overfeed.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh\n- `examples/catalog/2d/edge-work/edge-work.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh; edge-work cached moves regenerated\n- `examples/catalog/2d/first-part/first-part.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh; the pocket cache grows from 270 to 414 moves (the regenerated path), and the project file version moves to the current one\n- `examples/catalog/2d/hole-work/hole-work.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh; hole-work cached moves regenerated\n- `examples/catalog/2d/slots/slots.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh\n- `examples/catalog/3d/rough-finish/rough-finish.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh\n- `examples/catalog/multiaxis/indexed/indexed.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh\n- `examples/catalog/probing/probe-face/probe-face.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh\n- `examples/catalog/turning/bushing/bushing.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh\n- `examples/catalog/turning/cone-thread/cone-thread.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh\n- `examples/catalog/turning/contour-finishes/contour-finishes.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh; the turning contour cached paths regenerate\n- `examples/catalog/turning/groove-part-off/groove-part-off.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh\n- `examples/catalog/turning/taper-finish/taper-finish.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh\n- `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh by `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`; `.nc` byte-identical\n- `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh by `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`; `.nc` byte-identical\n- `examples/first-router-part.camproj` - stamp and cache refresh by `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`; `.nc` byte-identical\n\n`cargo xtask catalog --check` passes: 15 cases, including the expected refusals.\n\n## The part-off review fix\n\n`a_part_off_saved_before_3452_loads_stale_and_does_not_post` now reads the global version too: the saved-before-3452 groove beside the part-off loads Stale (its stamp carries the old `GENERATOR_OUTPUT_VERSION`), and the test regenerates both operations before the post runs. The historical unsafe fixture is unchanged: it still holds the old centred-kerf path, still loads Stale, and the post still refuses by name and writes no NC file until both ops are regenerated. The test also pins that the regenerated groove holds the same feed stations as the saved cache - the global version moved the stamp, not that path.\n\n## Pins\n\n`crates/app/src/operation/stamp_tests.rs`:\n- `a_bump_of_the_generator_output_version_moves_the_stamp` - version and version-1 digests differ; `current_stamp` stamps at the written version\n- `an_unchanged_generator_output_version_keeps_a_saved_cache_current` - the catalog contour-tabs case saved at the current version reloads Ok; nothing regenerates\n- `a_tabbed_contour_saved_before_the_bump_reads_stale` - the same case with its saved stamp rewritten to the pre-bump value: the loaded project reads Stale (never Ok), with the general stale reason, so the old cache can never post\n\n## Gate (final head, debug)\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib`: 321 passed (the 3 pins included).\n- The four refreshed suites: `continuous_4axis_part` (10 passed), `first_4axis_part` (4), `first_router_part` (4), `part_off_saved_before_3452` (2).\n- `example_catalog`: 44 passed, 4 ignored (heavy). `tool_after_state`: 5 passed.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check`: pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No motion/post generator change and no heavy or light lane (the fix is the staleness rule; the new tabbed start itself is pinned by #3684's `contour_tab_entry` tests).\n- No real pre-#3684 project file exists in the repo (PR #3684 regenerated the only one), so the pre-bump project is built by rewriting the saved stamp to the pre-bump digest - the `tool_after_state` house pattern for \"saved before\".\n- No UI run: the stale read is asserted through `operation::status_of` headlessly.\n\nChangelog: a generator defect fix that changes the emitted toolpath now makes every cached toolpath a project saved before it read stale once, so an old wrong move can never post silently.\n\nFixes #3704\n",
